<h1 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 3</h1>
<p style="text-align: center;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Environment and Recycling</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> In the Past, People Didn't Recycle as Much as They Do Now.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
    <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Present findings from a group discussion. Interactive: Engage in problem-solving conversations.</p>
      <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can present findings from a group discussion on sustainable living, comparing past and current practices through examples of daily habits (e.g., "Before, people threw everything away, but now they sort items for recycling and composting.")
Can engage in problem-solving conversations about sustainability by asking and responding to questions (e.g., "How can we save water?" "We can turn off the tap.")
Can ask and answer questions about sustainable practices, showing recognition of key discussion points (e.g., "What happens if we don't recycle?" "If we don't recycle, there will be more waste, and the water, soil, and atmosphere will be more polluted.").</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
  <thead>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
      <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows two images: one of a landfill from 30 years ago and one of a modern recycling facility. Students look at the images and discuss in pairs, "What differences do you see?" and "What do you think people did with waste in the past compared to now?" The teacher guides students to use expressions like "In the past, people..." and "Today, people..."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences comparing past and present practices, focusing on the target grammar (Past Simple vs. Present) and pronunciation of '-ed' endings. For example, the teacher says: "In the past, people <b>threw</b> all their waste away. (silent 'w' in threw). Today, we <b>sort</b> our waste. My grandparents <b>saved</b> old jars. (pronunciation /d/). We now <b>watched</b> many videos about recycling. (pronunciation /t/)." The teacher also models giving advice: "We <b>should</b> recycle more plastic."</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'In the past, people *didn't recycle*', does that mean they sorted trash or just threw it away?" (Expected answer: "They just threw it away.")</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'waste' mean? Is it something useful or something we throw away?" (Expected answer: "Something we throw away.")</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'saved' (with /d/ sound), am I talking about now or before?" (Expected answer: "Before.")</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Environment and Recycling".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio dialogue between a teenager (Maria) and her grandmother (Elena) discussing how environmental practices have changed in their town over the years. The dialogue includes phrases like "In the past, we didn't think about sorting waste, we just had one bin for everything," "Today, we reduce, reuse, and recycle," "If we waste water, there will be less for everyone," and "You should always turn off the tap." (Authentic dialogue, conversational register, audio format).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will understand main points and specific details in short, clear audio messages about past and present environmental practices, to prepare for speaking about them.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Speaking focus):</b> The teacher plays the audio twice.</p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> After the first listening, students turn to a partner and verbally answer: "What are Maria and Elena talking about?" "What is the main difference they mention?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (spoken):</b> After the second listening, the teacher states sentences, and students verbally respond "True" or "False," justifying their answers:
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In the past, people *often recycled* plastic bottles." (False, they *didn't recycle* that much)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Elena thinks we *should save* water." (True)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we *don't protect* the environment, the planet will be *cleaner*." (False, it will be *more polluted*).</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-10 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Practicing Past Simple vs. present practices, First Conditional, and Modal 'should' to discuss environmental habits. Using vocabulary: recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, important, carefully, often. Focused pronunciation of '-ed' endings (/d/, /ɪd/, /t/).</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice - Sentence Chunks (Pair Work):</b> The teacher provides sentence beginnings and students complete them orally in pairs, focusing on the correct verb tense and vocabulary. They read their completed sentences aloud.
            <ul>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"In the past, people didn't _______________ that much." (recycle / save energy)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, people are more aware of the importance of _______________." (recycling / protecting the environment)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we waste water, there _______________." (will be less for everyone)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You should _______________ when brushing your teeth." (turn off the tap)</li>
              <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Teacher monitors for pronunciation of '-ed' endings, e.g., 'wanted' /ɪd/, 'saved' /d/, 'watched' /t/ as students complete relevant sentences verbally.)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled - "Advice Chain":</b> Students sit in a circle. The first student starts with an environmental problem (e.g., "There is too much plastic waste in our community."). The next student gives advice using 'should' and the first conditional (e.g., "We should reduce plastic. If we reduce plastic, there will be less pollution."). The next student contrasts past and present practices (e.g., "In the past, people didn't think about plastic waste, but today we know it's important to recycle."). The chain continues, ensuring each student speaks.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction - "Past vs. Present Habits":</b> Students work in new pairs. They interview each other about their family's past and present daily habits related to recycling, water use, and energy saving. They use prompts like: "What did your family do to save energy in the past?" "How do you save water today?" "What happens if we don't recycle glass?" "What should we do to protect our planet?" Students should aim to use all three target grammar points and relevant vocabulary.</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-20 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Environment and Recycling".</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: "Our Community's Environmental Challenge - Then and Now"</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in groups of 3-4. Each group is assigned a specific local environmental issue (e.g., plastic litter in the schoolyard, water waste in homes, excessive energy consumption). Their task is to:</p>
        <ol>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Discuss how people managed this issue in the past (e.g., "In the past, students threw plastic bottles anywhere.").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Discuss current practices and the impact (e.g., "Today, some still waste energy. If we waste energy, our electricity bill will be higher, and it harms the environment.").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Propose solutions and give advice to their peers/community using 'should' and the first conditional (e.g., "We should organize recycling bins in every classroom. If we recycle, we will reduce waste and protect our planet.").</li>
        </ol>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Each group will then present their findings and proposed solutions to the class. They should make sure to highlight differences between past and present, express cause-effect relationships, and offer clear advice. The teacher circulates, facilitating discussion and listening for accurate use of target grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation (stress contrasts and '-ed' endings).</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group presentations and peer assessment. The teacher notes down examples of successful use of target language and areas needing improvement.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group's oral presentation from Stage 4. Students will listen to other groups and complete a simple peer assessment sheet.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially '-ed' endings and stress contrasts between past/present verbs).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Past Simple vs. Present practices (e.g., "In the past, people didn't recycle that much." "Today people are more aware...").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of First Conditional (e.g., "If we waste water, there will be less for everyone.").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of Modal 'should' for giving advice (e.g., "You should turn off the tap...").</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (recycle, waste, environment, pollution, reduce, save, protect, etc.).</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of presenting findings and solutions.</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and engagement in problem-solving conversation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete individually:</p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new thing you learned to say today about protecting the environment?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Give one piece of advice you heard today that you can use at home."</li>
        </ul>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompts:</b></p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you find easy or difficult when comparing past and present environmental habits in your group's discussion?"</li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you use sentences with 'If... then...' and 'should' to talk about saving our planet in your daily life?"</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students effectively used Past Simple to describe past practices and 'should' for advice. The first conditional still needs some reinforcement, especially in spontaneous speech; some students confused its structure or verb tenses. Pronunciation of '-ed' endings was generally good, but 'watched' /t/ and 'saved' /d/ still had slight difficulties for some. The group problem-solving aspect worked well, fostering collaboration. For the next lesson (Writing), I need to provide more structured sentence starters for the first conditional and encourage varied vocabulary usage in written responses, reinforcing the spoken practice from today.</p>
        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson's discussions on comparing past/present practices and proposing solutions will directly feed into the writing task for Lesson 4, where students will compose short paragraphs detailing an environmental problem and its solutions, using the grammar and vocabulary practiced today.</p>
      </td>
      <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>